    "note": "Net issuance = bond proceeds − repayments, trailing twelve months, summed over Microsoft, Alphabet, Amazon, Meta and Oracle (SEC EDGAR cash-flow statements; includes their EUR/CHF/GBP issues). US corporate market = Fed Z.1 net bond issuance of all US nonfinancial corporations (all ratings) — gross US IG issuance (SIFMA) is not freely downloadable, so both sides are measured net. Not shown when the market's net issuance is below $100bn (e.g. 2022, when corporates were net repaying). Treasury = change in debt held by the public over the same 12 months (Treasury Fiscal Data). Oracle's fiscal quarters (ending Feb/May/Aug/Nov) are mapped to the calendar quarter they end in.",
    "spreadNote": "Proxy, not issuer-level spreads: ICE BofA US Corporate option-adjusted spread indices by rating bucket, matched to each hyperscaler's S&P/Moody's rating (Microsoft AAA/Aaa; Alphabet, Amazon, Meta AA range; Oracle BBB). Individual bonds trade around their bucket — e.g. a heavy new issuer can price wider than its rating peers. Source: ICE Data Indices via FRED, which only carries the last 3 years of history."
